1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Bd3?! { Looks natural, but ...Bxd3 trades off Black's problem piece for White's good one. The right move is 4.Nf3. } 4... Bxd3 5. Qxd3 e6 { Black has swapped away the bishop that e5 was cramping, and can now break with ...c5 and ...Nc6 in comfort. } *
